<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-12>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-12" ;
    dcterms:title "Base64 variant of kid in the DID trustlist is unspecified" ;
    dcterms:description """The DID trustlist uses a "base64 encoded key id" as the verification method fragment and as JWK kid. It does not say whether that is standard or URL-safe base64, or whether padding is kept. Standard and URL-safe base64 differ on '+' and '/', and the PR example kid WHM+BYqqZiE= contains '+'.""" ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/did-examples> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-A.1> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-13>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-13" ;
    dcterms:title "Mapping between GDHCN participant codes (alpha-3) and iss (alpha-2)" ;
    dcterms:description "Participant codes are ISO 3166-1 alpha-3, while iss and the X.509 C attribute use alpha-2. The test pair XXA/XX is user-assigned and not a formal ISO mapping. A verifier narrowing trust-list lookups by iss needs an authoritative mapping." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-12.3> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-3.2.4> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/doc-vs-participants> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-14>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-14" ;
    dcterms:title "Package coordinates and licence for the libraries" ;
    dcterms:description "Maven group / Kotlin package root and crate names are placeholders. The natural reverse-DNS root, int.who, cannot be used because `int` is a reserved Java keyword. The licence has not been chosen." ;
    stt:upstreamFix false ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-languages> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-15>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-15" ;
    dcterms:title "Asynchronous crypto and I/O across the WIT boundary" ;
    dcterms:description "WASI 0.2 component calls are synchronous. WebCrypto (the natural crypto backend for Kotlin/JS on Node and browsers) is promise-based, as are remote KMS signers and HTTP fetches. The design avoids async callbacks into the host: signing is two-phase and trust lists are loaded by the host. The Rust component verifies with in-WASM RustCrypto, so verify stays synchronous. Kotlin/JS must either use Node's synchronous `crypto` module (Node only) or expose a Promise-returning verify, which would diverge from the jco surface. Decide before implementation; revisit when WASI 0.3 async is stable." ;
    stt:upstreamFix false ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-wit> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-webcrypto> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-16>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-16" ;
    dcterms:title "WIT type-system limits" ;
    dcterms:description "WIT has no recursive types, so generic CBOR crosses as encoded bytes and only DVCMin and VHL are typed records. s64 becomes bigint in JavaScript, so it is used only for NumericDate, and subclaim numbers are s32. result<T, E> is thrown as ComponentError by jco, so APIs whose failures are expected (verify) return a variant instead." ;
    stt:upstreamFix false ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-wit> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-17>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-17" ;
    dcterms:title "The example issues an abstract logical model" ;
    dcterms:description "In smart-trust-phw, DVCMin and DVCMinVaccineDetails are declared abstract (^abstract = true). Only DVCMinPreQual and DVCMinVaccineDetailsPreQual are concrete. The HCert logical model puts DVCMin at subclaim -6, and the PR 129 example issues a DVCMin with ICD-11 codes. So no concrete model exists for a non-PreQual DVC: either DVCMin should not be abstract, or a concrete ICD-11 profile is needed." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-dvcmin> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-dvcmin-vx> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-dvcmin-prequal> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-3> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-12.4> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-18>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-18" ;
    dcterms:title "Sex binding in DVCMin points at a CodeSystem, not a ValueSet" ;
    dcterms:description "DVCMin.s is bound (extensible) to $GENDER, which smart-trust-phw aliases to http://hl7.org/fhir/administrative-gender, the CodeSystem URL. A binding must reference a ValueSet: http://hl7.org/fhir/ValueSet/administrative-gender." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-dvcmin> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-phw-aliases> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-19>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-19" ;
    dcterms:title "Upstream home for the CDDL and JSON-LD artefacts" ;
    dcterms:description "The HCERT envelope CDDL (api/cddl/hcert.cddl) belongs in WorldHealthOrganization/smart-trust next to the HCERT Specification, which owns the wire format. The payload JSON-LD context, SHACL and CDDL belong with their logical models in smart-trust-phw, ideally generated by the IG build and published at the canonical URL. They are drafted here until upstream adopts them." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-3.2.1> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/ext-dvcmin> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-20>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-20" ;
    dcterms:title "CDDL validator deviations (cddl-rs / pycddl)" ;
    dcterms:description "The only Python CDDL validator, pycddl (wrapping the Rust cddl crate), deviates from RFC 8610 in four ways found here: .cbor inside arrays is applied to the wrong items; .regexp is not implicitly anchored; escaped regex classes such as \\s are treated as literals; and map closure is not enforced across group-choice alternatives. The CDDL files stay spec-correct, and tools/check_models.py works around the first three. The schema avoids relying on the fourth. Cross-check with a second validator (e.g. cddlc) before upstreaming." ;
    stt:upstreamFix false ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-rfc8610> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-rfc9682> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-001>
    a stt:Requirement ;
    dcterms:identifier "STT-GEN-001" ;
    dcterms:title "Issuance and verification of the full HCERT QR pipeline" ;
    stt:statement "The library SHALL implement issuance (steps 1 to 9) and verification (QR Code Generation section 11) of HCERT QR codes." ;
    stt:conformance "SHALL" ;
    stt:category "scope" ;
    stt:derivationType "derived" ;
    stt:target "kotlin" ;
    stt:target "rust" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-1> ;
    stt:hasDerivation <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-001/derivation/1> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-1> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-2> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-3> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-4> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-5> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-6> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-7> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-8> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-9> ;
    stt:implementsStep <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/step-verify> ;
    stt:satisfies <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/IssuerVDHC-generate> ;
    stt:satisfies <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/IssuerVDHC-sign> ;
    stt:satisfies <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/UtilizeVDHC-validate-hash> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-issuer> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-verifier> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-001/derivation/1>
    a stt:Derivation ;
    stt:source <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-1> ;
    stt:quote "Steps 3 to 9 never vary. A verifier runs the same list upwards." .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-002>
    a stt:Requirement ;
    dcterms:identifier "STT-GEN-002" ;
    dcterms:title "Every step callable on its own" ;
    stt:statement "Each pipeline step SHALL be exposed as a separate public operation (payload codec, CWT build, CBOR, COSE sign/parse, ZLIB, Base45, HC1 prefix, QR) as well as through the end-to-end issuer and verifier, so that integrators can substitute or inspect any stage." ;
    stt:conformance "SHALL" ;
    stt:category "architecture" ;
    stt:derivationType "derived" ;
    stt:target "kotlin" ;
    stt:target "rust" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-1> ;
    stt:hasDerivation <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-002/derivation/1> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-intro> ;
    stt:hasDerivation <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-002/derivation/2> ;
    stt:refines <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-001> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-cbor> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-sign1> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-zlib> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-base45> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-hc1> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-qr> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-002/derivation/1>
    a stt:Derivation ;
    stt:source <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-1> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-002/derivation/2>
    a stt:Derivation ;
    stt:source <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-intro> ;
    stt:quote "The first step below is therefore a selection step, and everything after it is mechanical." .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-003>
    a stt:Requirement ;
    dcterms:identifier "STT-GEN-003" ;
    dcterms:title "Payload-agnostic core" ;
    stt:statement "The modules for steps 3 to 9 SHALL NOT depend on any payload logical model. Payloads SHALL be plugged in through a PayloadCodec registered against a subclaim." ;
    stt:conformance "SHALL" ;
    stt:category "architecture" ;
    stt:derivationType "derived" ;
    stt:target "kotlin" ;
    stt:target "rust" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-intro> ;
    stt:hasDerivation <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-003/derivation/1> ;
    stt:refines <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-001> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-payload-codec> ;
    stt:constrainsApi <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/api-subclaim-registry> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-003/derivation/1>
    a stt:Derivation ;
    stt:source <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-intro> ;
    stt:quote "The container, the signature and the transport encoding are the same for every GDHCN trust domain ... What changes from one use case to the next is only the payload" .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-004>
    a stt:Requirement ;
    dcterms:identifier "STT-GEN-004" ;
    dcterms:title "Kotlin first, for JVM, Android and Node" ;
    stt:statement "The first implementation SHALL be a Kotlin Multiplatform library with all pipeline logic in common code. It SHALL ship for three targets: JVM (Java 11+), Android, and Node.js (Kotlin/JS IR, published to npm with an @JsExport facade and generated TypeScript declarations). Other KMP targets MAY follow." ;
    stt:conformance "SHALL" ;
    stt:category "non-functional" ;
    stt:derivationType "directive" ;
    stt:target "kotlin" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-languages> ;
    stt:hasDerivation <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/STT-GEN-004/derivation/1> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-targets> ;
